# Home Page and Theme Conventions

The home page is a `mode: custom` MDX layout built with Tailwind classes.
Mintlify loads every root-level `.css` and `.js` file automatically, so
`style.css`, `academy.css`, and `search.js` need no registration.

## Structure

```text
index.mdx                      # mode: custom; composes the intro, preview, and guide grid
snippets/home-content.jsx      # section links and guide cards
snippets/home-academy.jsx      # Academy preview player
snippets/home-guide-grid.jsx   # guide cards
style.css                      # app shell colors, topbar pills, sidebar tweaks (theme.css overrides)
home.css                       # home layout, scoped to .help-home
academy.css                    # Academy card outline and sidebar duration tag
search.js                      # wires data-search-trigger to Mintlify's own search button
sidebar.js                     # empty Settings sidebar title; Mintlify drops a group with no pages
```

## Patterns

- `index.mdx` uses Tailwind utilities with `dark:` variants for every color.
  Icons are Hugeicons from `assets/icons/`, set with
  `<Icon src="/assets/icons/<name>.svg" />`. No Lucide names.
- The custom search button carries `data-search-trigger`; `search.js`
  forwards clicks to Mintlify's `#search-bar-entry` (and its `-mobile`
  variant).
- `index.mdx` only composes the page. A snippet cannot import another
  snippet, and a capitalized tag inside a snippet is read as a Mintlify
  component, so `HomeAcademyFeature` receives `renderVideo` and an `icon`
  element from the page. Keep helpers inside the exported component;
  Mintlify drops other declarations in a snippet file. These snippets are
  home-only.
- Guide cards come from `homeGuides` in `snippets/home-content.jsx`, one per
  Guides sidebar group.
  Each card links to an overview article and shows the same screen as that
  article's first screenshot, from `assets/images/home/<card>.webp` (and
  `-dark`), inside a 1px border with `noZoom`. The images come from the
  `corner` template in `diamond-screenshots` (`recipes/help-centre/home.mjs`);
  recapture them there instead of cropping in CSS.
- Use `<div role="navigation">` for link rows; Mintlify drops `<nav>` from MDX.
- CSS overrides target Mintlify's stable ids and classes
  (`#content-container`, `.nav-logo`, `#search-bar-entry`) and use
  `!important` only where the theme already sets the property. Keep a comment
  above each block naming what it overrides and why.
- Light and dark values sit next to each other: `.selector {}` then
  `.dark .selector {}`.

## Boundaries

- No content in `index.mdx` beyond entry points; articles live in the tabs.
- No feature-specific CSS in `style.css`; Academy styling stays in
  `academy.css`, and a new feature file gets its own `<name>.css`.
- No DOM changes in `search.js` other than click forwarding. Do not replace
  Mintlify's search.
- Do not add a third root JS file without a comment explaining what it hooks.
  `eslint.config.js` is editor tooling and is listed in `.mintignore`.
